---
// Section 2: THE REALITY CHECK — Editorial Flow
---

<section id="problem" class="scroll-mt-24 py-24 md:py-32 bg-[#060709] border-y border-white/[0.06] relative overflow-hidden">
  <!-- Subtle ambient glow -->
  <div class="pointer-events-none absolute -top-40 left-1/4 w-96 h-96 bg-[#FF2D55]/5 rounded-full blur-[140px]"></div>

  <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6">
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-12 gap-12 lg:gap-16 items-start">
      
      <!-- Left Column: Core Insight & Philosophy -->
      <div class="lg:col-span-5 space-y-6 text-left sticky top-28">
        <div class="inline-block telemetry-pill text-[#FF2D55] bg-[#FF2D55]/10 border-[#FF2D55]/30">
          THE REALITY CHECK
        </div>
        
        <h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl lg:text-5xl font-black text-white tracking-tight leading-tight">
          Saving is instant.<br />
          <span class="text-[#8E9196] font-normal">Finding it again is impossible.</span>
        </h2>

        <!-- Discovery-to-Action Philosophy Quote -->
        <blockquote class="p-5 rounded-2xl bg-white/[0.03] border-l-2 border-[#FF2D55] text-sm sm:text-base text-white/90 leading-relaxed font-medium">
          "Social feeds are built for discovery and continuous browsing. STASH is built for what happens after you find something worth keeping."
        </blockquote>

        <p class="text-sm text-[#9CA3AF] leading-relaxed">
          You save a recipe on Tuesday feeling inspired. On Saturday at the grocery store, you stand in the aisle scrolling through hundreds of unorganized bookmarks trying to locate it. Social bookmarks are silos—designed to keep you scrolling, not to help you do what you saved.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Right Column: Editorial Typographic Hierarchy (Not 3 Equal Cards) -->
      <div class="lg:col-span-7 space-y-10 text-left pt-2 lg:pt-8">
        
        <!-- Point 01 -->
        <div class="border-b border-white/[0.08] pb-8 space-y-2">
          <div class="font-mono text-xs text-[#FF2D55] font-bold tracking-wider">01</div>
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-black text-white tracking-tight">Saved everywhere.</h3>
          <p class="text-neutral-400 text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed max-w-lg">
            Your best finds are scattered across TikTok, Instagram, YouTube, and screenshots. None of them talk to each other.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Point 02 -->
        <div class="border-b border-white/[0.08] pb-8 space-y-2">
          <div class="font-mono text-xs text-[#FF2D55] font-bold tracking-wider">02</div>
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-black text-white tracking-tight">Buried by the next scroll.</h3>
          <p class="text-neutral-400 text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed max-w-lg">
            The thing you saved last week gets buried by everything you save today. Feeds are built to keep you moving forward, not looking back.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Point 03: Elevated Typographic Weight & Breathing Room -->
        <div class="pt-2 p-6 rounded-3xl bg-gradient-to-br from-white/[0.04] to-transparent border border-white/[0.08] space-y-3">
          <div class="font-mono text-xs text-[#10B981] font-bold tracking-wider">03</div>
          <h3 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-black text-white tracking-tight leading-snug">
            A save isn’t a plan.
          </h3>
          <p class="text-neutral-300 text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed max-w-lg">
            A recipe, workout, or tutorial only matters when you can actually use it. Bookmarks don't become dinner or gym sessions on their own.
          </p>
          <div class="pt-2 text-xs font-mono text-[#10B981] flex items-center gap-2">
            <span>↓</span>
            <span>That’s why STASH exists</span>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>
